   Yep.  What that message means is that when the game restored your
savefile, there was a monster in it who was marked as "wielding a weapon".
However, none of that monster's inventory items were marked as "being
wielded." So the game prints that message to let you know that something
is amiss, and then it takes away the monster's weapon and plows ahead
as if nothing had happened.
   That message means either someone's been tampering with your savefile,
or it got corrupted on disk somehow, or there was a bug in the program
when you saved your game last time.

   Does your Nethack have any patches installed? If so, maybe one of
them has a bug. Otherwise, I give it 50/50 whether it's a bug in Nethack
or a tampered-with-or-corrupted savefile.

   Anyway, as you discovered, the game will plow ahead merrily, and if
you don't notice anything weird, then it's probably all right.

